# Agent OS — SpectraSynq K1 Firmware

Read [`AGENT_OS.md`](../../AGENT_OS.md) before any task in this repo. It is the
canonical, tool-agnostic manual for all agents (Devin, Claude Code, Codex,
Cursor).

## Minimum before acting

1. Run `bash scripts/agent/session-bootstrap.sh` — must exit 0. If it exits
   nonzero, `repo-truth.sh` reported FAIL; resolve before proceeding.
2. Read `AGENT_OS.md` — source-of-truth hierarchy, current lane, safety rules,
   thinking gate, skill awareness gate.
3. Keyword-scan `available_skills` for a skill that fits the task domain.
4. If the task involves **resume / prior work / memory / "did we already" /
   history**, apply the **claude-mem scenario table** below (or invoke
   `/claude-mem-router`) — pick **one** skill, do not fan out the set.
5. For decisions/architecture/debugging-under-uncertainty, invoke
   `/thinking-model-router` before acting.

## Hard rules (from AGENT_OS.md)

- Never say a result does not mean ship / promote / close without the remaining numbered ship path in the same answer (`/ship-path-required`, Captain 2026-08-17).
- No firmware source edits unless explicitly scoped.
- No `platformio.ini` env behavior changes unless explicitly scoped.
- No flash / upload / erase / serial monitor without explicit approval.
- No `start_noise_cal` without confirmed silence.
- Build via `bash scripts/agent/pio-build.sh <env>` only (wrapper rejects
  upload/monitor tokens). Allowed envs: `k1_hardware`, `k1_bench_reference`,
  `k1_bench_im73d`.
- Commit only after the pre-commit gate passes (pytest + pio build for the
  changed class).
- End session with `scripts/agent/post-session-report.md` filled (including
  `thinking_skill_used`, `skills_used`, `specialists_used`).

## Claude-mem scenario → skill (always-on reference)

| Scenario | Skill |
|----------|-------|
| Current lane / device / branch; before flash/forensics | `/spec-recall` |
| "Did we already fix X?" / prior bug / recurrence | `/mem-search` |
| Code structure without full-file reads | `/smart-explore` |
| Cold-start / prime unfamiliar tree | `/learn-codebase` |
| Theme corpus Q&A | `/knowledge-agent` |
| One sweeping journey report | `/timeline-report` |
| Week-by-week serial chapters | `/weekly-digests` |
| How the memory tool works | `/how-it-works` |
| Memory empty/stale/offline/contradicts Tier 0 | `/memory-authority-gate` |
| Unsure which of the above | `/claude-mem-router` |

**Default K1 ladder:** bootstrap → `/spec-recall` → `/mem-search` (2–4 single-term
queries) → act from git + on-disk + filtered observations → record observations.

On-disk handover beats claude-mem for **current** lane status. Full playbook:
`.cursor/skills/claude-mem-router/SKILL.md` (also in `.claude/skills/` and
`.codex/skills/`). Refresh: `bash scripts/install-claude-mem-skills.sh`.

## Cursor-specific

Cursor skills live in `.cursor/skills/`. The same specialist agents and
claude-mem MCP available to Claude Code are available here. Tool-specific
overlays for other tools are listed in `AGENT_OS.md` → "Tool-specific overlays".
